\mt1 Ephesians
\c 1
\s1 Paul’s Greeting to the Ephesians
\r (\ref Acts 19:8–12|ACT 19:8-12\ref*; \ref Revelation 2:1–7|REV 2:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 1 Paul, an apostle of Christ Jesus by \add the\add* will of God,
\p To the saints in Ephesus,\f + \fr 1:1 \ft Some manuscripts do not include \fqa in Ephesus\ft .\f* \add the\add* faithful in Christ Jesus:
\p \v 2 Grace and peace to you from God our Father and \add the\add* Lord Jesus Christ.
\s1 Spiritual Blessings
\r (\ref Romans 8:28–34|ROM 8:28-34\ref*)
\p \v 3 Blessed \add be\add* the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who has blessed us in Christ with every spiritual blessing in the heavenly realms. \v 4 For He chose us in Him before \add the\add* foundation of \add the\add* world to be holy and blameless in His presence. In love \v 5 He predestined us for adoption as His sons through Jesus Christ, according to the good pleasure of His will, \v 6 to \add the\add* praise of His glorious grace, which He has freely given us in the Beloved \add One\add*.
\p \v 7 In \add Him\add* we have redemption through His blood, the forgiveness of our trespasses, according to the riches of His grace \v 8 that He lavished on us with all wisdom and understanding. \v 9 \add And\add* He has made known to us the mystery of His will according to His good pleasure, which He purposed in \add Christ\add* \v 10 as a plan for the fullness of time, to bring all things in heaven and on earth \add together\add* in Christ.
\p \v 11 In Him we were also chosen as God’s own, having been predestined according to \add the\add* plan of \add Him who\add* works out everything by the counsel of His will, \v 12 in order that we, who were the first to hope in Christ, would be for \add the\add* praise of His glory.
\p \v 13 And in \add Him\add*, having heard and believed the word of truth — the gospel of your salvation — you were sealed with the promised Holy Spirit, \v 14 who is \add the\add* pledge of our inheritance until \add the\add* redemption of those \add who are God’s\add* possession, to \add the\add* praise of His glory.
\s1 Spiritual Wisdom
\r (\ref 1 Corinthians 2:6–16|1CO 2:6-16\ref*)
\p \v 15 For this reason, ever since I heard about your faith in the Lord Jesus and \add your\add* love for all the saints, \v 16 \add I have\add* not stopped giving thanks for you, remembering you in my prayers, \v 17 that the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the glorious Father, may give you \add a\add* spirit of wisdom and revelation in \add your\add* knowledge of Him.
\p \v 18 \add I ask that\add* the eyes of your heart\f + \fr 1:18 \ft TR \fqa the eyes of your understanding\f* may be enlightened, so that you may know the hope of His calling, the riches of His glorious inheritance in the saints, \v 19 and the surpassing greatness of His power to us who believe.  \add These are \add* in accordance with the working of His mighty strength, \v 20 which He exerted in Christ when He raised Him from \add the\add* dead and seated \add Him\add* at His right hand in the heavenly realms, \v 21 far above all rule and authority, power and dominion, and every name that is named, not only in the present age but also in the \add one\add* to come.
\p \v 22 And \add God\add* put everything under His feet and made Him head over everything for the church, \v 23 which is His body, the fullness of \add Him\add* who fills all in all.
\c 2
\s1 Alive with Christ
\r (\ref Colossians 2:6–23|COL 2:6-23\ref*)
\p \v 1 And you were dead in your trespasses and sins, \v 2 in which you used to walk when you conformed to the ways of this world \add and\add* of the ruler of the power of the air, the spirit \add who is\add* now at work in the sons of disobedience. \v 3 All of us also lived among \add them\add* at one time, fulfilling the cravings of our flesh \add and\add* indulging \add its\add* desires and thoughts. Like the rest, we were by nature children of wrath.
\p \v 4 But because of His great love for us, God, who is rich in mercy, \v 5 made \add us\add* alive with Christ even when we were dead in our trespasses. \add It is\add* by grace you have been saved! \v 6 And \add God\add* raised \add us\add* up with \add Christ\add* and seated \add us with Him\add* in the heavenly realms in Christ Jesus, \v 7 in order that in the coming ages He might display the surpassing riches of His grace, \add demonstrated\add* by \add His\add* kindness to us in Christ Jesus.
\p \v 8 For \add it is\add* by grace you have been saved through faith, and this not from yourselves; \add it is\add* the gift of God, \v 9 not by works, so that no one can boast. \v 10 For we are \add God’s\add* workmanship, created in Christ Jesus to do good works, which God prepared in advance as our way of life.\f + \fr 2:10 \ft Literally \fqa which God prepared beforehand, that we should walk in them.\f*
\s1 One in Christ
\r (\ref Philippians 2:1–4|PHP 2:1-4\ref*)
\p \v 11 Therefore remember that formerly you who \add are\add* Gentiles in \add the\add* flesh \add and\add* called uncircumcised by the so-called circumcision (\add that done\add* in \add the\add* body by human hands) — \v 12 \add remember\add* that at that time you were separate from Christ, alienated from the commonwealth of Israel, and strangers to the covenants of the promise, without hope and without God in the world. \v 13 But now in Christ Jesus you who once were far away have been brought near through the blood of Christ.
\p \v 14 For He Himself is our peace, who has made the two one and has torn down the dividing wall of hostility \v 15 by abolishing in His flesh the law of commandments \add and\add* decrees. \add He did this \add* to create in Himself one new man \add out of\add* the two, \add thus\add* making peace \v 16 and reconciling both \add of them\add* to God in one body through the cross, by which He put to death \add their\add* hostility.
\p \v 17 He came \add and\add* preached peace to you who \add were\add* far away and peace to those \add who were\add* near. \v 18 For through Him we both have access to the Father by one Spirit.
\s1 Christ Our Cornerstone
\r (\ref Isaiah 28:14–22|ISA 28:14-22\ref*; \ref 1 Corinthians 3:10–15|1CO 3:10-15\ref*; \ref 1 Peter 2:1–8|1PE 2:1-8\ref*)
\p \v 19 Therefore you are no longer strangers and foreigners, but fellow citizens with the saints and members of God’s household, \v 20 built on the foundation of the apostles and prophets, \add with\add* Christ Jesus Himself as \add the\add* cornerstone. \v 21 In Him the whole building is fitted together \add and\add* grows into a holy temple in \add the\add* Lord. \v 22 \add And\add* in \add Him\add* you too \add are\add* being built together into a dwelling place for God in \add His\add* Spirit.
\c 3
\s1 The Mystery of the Gospel
\p \v 1 For this reason I, Paul, the prisoner of Christ Jesus for the sake of you Gentiles...\f + \fr 3:1 \ft This train of thought is continued in verse 14.\f*
\p \v 2 Surely you have heard about the stewardship of God’s grace that was given to me for you, \v 3 that \add is\add*, the mystery made known to me by revelation, as I have already written briefly. \v 4 In reading this, then, you will be able to understand my insight into the mystery of Christ, \v 5 which was not made known to men in other generations as it has now been revealed by \add the\add* Spirit to \add God’s\add* holy apostles and prophets. \v 6 \add This mystery is that\add* through the gospel the Gentiles are fellow heirs, fellow members of the body, and fellow partakers of the promise in Christ Jesus.
\p \v 7 I became a servant of \add this gospel\add* by the gift of God’s grace, given me through the working of His power. \v 8 \add Though I am\add* less than the least of all \add the\add* saints, this grace was given me: to preach to the Gentiles the unsearchable riches of Christ, \v 9 and to illuminate for everyone the stewardship\f + \fr 3:9 \ft NE and WH \fqa and to illuminate the stewardship\ft ; TR \fqa and to illuminate for everyone the fellowship\f* of \add this\add* mystery, which for ages past was kept hidden in God, who created all things. \v 10  \add His purpose was \add* that now, through the church, the manifold wisdom of God should be made known to the rulers and authorities in the heavenly realms, \v 11 according to \add the\add* eternal purpose that He accomplished in Christ Jesus our Lord.
\p \v 12 In Him \add and\add* through faith in Him\f + \fr 3:12 \ft Or \fqa through His faithfulness\f* we may enter  \add God’s \add* presence with boldness and confidence. \v 13 So I ask \add you\add* not to be discouraged because of my sufferings for you, which are your glory.
\s1 Paul’s Prayer for the Ephesians
\p \v 14 ... for this reason I bow my knees before the Father,\f + \fr 3:14 \ft BYZ and TR \fqa before the Father of our Lord Jesus Christ,\f* \v 15 from whom every family in heaven and on earth derives its name. \v 16 \add I ask\add* that out of the riches of His glory He may strengthen you with power through His Spirit in \add your\add* inner being, \v 17 so that Christ may dwell in your hearts through faith. \add Then\add* you, being rooted and grounded in love, \v 18 will have power, together with all the saints, to comprehend the length and width and height and depth \v 19 of the love of Christ, and to know \add this love that\add* surpasses knowledge, that you may be filled with all the fullness of God.
\p \v 20 Now to \add Him\add* who is able to do immeasurably more than all we ask or imagine, according to \add His\add* power that \add is\add* at work within us, \v 21 to Him \add be\add* the glory in the church and in Christ Jesus throughout all generations, forever \add and\add* ever. Amen.
\c 4
\s1 Unity in the Body
\r (\ref Psalm 133:1–3|PSA 133:1-3\ref*; \ref 1 Corinthians 1:10–17|1CO 1:10-17\ref*)
\p \v 1 \add As a\add* prisoner in \add the\add* Lord, then, I urge you to walk in a manner worthy of the calling you have received: \v 2 with all humility and gentleness, with patience, bearing with one another in love, \v 3 \add and\add* with diligence to preserve the unity of the Spirit through the bond of peace.
\p \v 4 \add There is\add* one body and one Spirit, just as you were called to one hope \add when\add* you were called; \v 5 one Lord, one faith, one baptism; \v 6 one God and Father of all, who \add is\add* over all and through all and in all.
\p \v 7 Now to each one of us grace has been given according to the measure of the gift of Christ. \v 8 This is why it says:\f + \fr 4:8 \ft Or \fqa He says\f*
\b 
\q1 “When He ascended on high,
\q2 He led captives away,
\q2 and gave gifts to men.”\f + \fr 4:8 \ref Psalm 68:18|PSA 68:18\ref*\f*
\p \v 9 What \add does\add* “He ascended” \add mean\add*, except that He also descended\f + \fr 4:9 \ft BYZ and TR \fqa except that He also descended first\f* to the lower parts of the earth? \v 10 He who descended is the very \add One\add* who ascended above all the heavens, in order to fill all things.
\p \v 11 And \add it was\add* He who gave some \add to be\add* apostles, some \add to be\add* prophets, some \add to be\add* evangelists, and some \add to be\add* pastors and teachers, \v 12 to equip the saints for works of ministry \add and\add* to build up the body of Christ, \v 13 until we all reach unity in the faith and in the knowledge of the Son of God, \add as we\add* mature to the full measure of \add the\add* stature of Christ.
\p \v 14 Then \add we will\add* no longer be infants, tossed about by the waves and carried around by every wind of teaching \add and\add* by the clever cunning of men in \add their\add* deceitful scheming. \v 15 Instead, speaking the truth in love, \add we will\add* in all things grow up into Christ Himself, who is the head. \v 16 From \add Him\add* the whole body, fitted and held together by every supporting ligament, grows \add and\add* builds itself up in love through \add the\add* work of each individual part.
\s1 New Life in Christ
\r (\ref Colossians 3:1–17|COL 3:1-17\ref*)
\p \v 17 So I tell \add you\add* this, and insist \add on it\add* in \add the\add* Lord, \add that\add* you \add must\add* no longer walk as the Gentiles do, in \add the\add* futility of their thinking. \v 18 They are darkened in \add their\add* understanding \add and\add* alienated from the life of God because of the ignorance that is in them due to the hardness of their hearts. \v 19 Having lost all sense of shame, \add they\add* have given themselves over to sensuality for \add the\add* practice of every kind of impurity, with a craving for more.
\p \v 20 But this is not the way you came to know Christ. \v 21 Surely you heard of Him and were taught in Him— in keeping with \add the\add* truth that is in Jesus— \v 22 to put off your former way of life, \add your\add* old self, which is being corrupted by \add its\add* deceitful desires; \v 23 to be renewed in the spirit of your minds; \v 24 and to put on the new self, created to be like God in true righteousness and holiness.
\p \v 25 Therefore each \add of you\add* must put off falsehood \add and\add* speak truthfully to his neighbor, for we are all members of one another. \v 26 “Be angry, yet \add do\add* not sin.”\f + \fr 4:26 \ft Or \fqa “In your anger do not sin.”\ref Psalm 4:4|PSA 4:4\ref*\f* \add Do\add* not \add let\add* the sun set upon your anger, \v 27 \add and do\add* not give the devil a foothold.
\p \v 28 He who has been stealing must steal no longer, but must work, doing good with \add his\add* own hands, that he may have \add something\add* to share with the \add one in\add* need.
\p \v 29 \add Let\add* no unwholesome talk come out of your mouths, but only what is helpful for building up the \add one\add* in need \add and\add* bringing grace to those who listen.
\p \v 30 And \add do\add* not grieve the Holy Spirit of God, in whom you were sealed for \add the\add* day of redemption.
\p \v 31 Get rid of all bitterness, rage and anger, outcry and slander, along with every form of malice. \v 32 Be kind \add and\add* tenderhearted to one another, forgiving each other just as in Christ God forgave you.
\c 5
\s1 Imitators of God
\p \v 1 Be imitators of God, therefore, as beloved children, \v 2 and walk in love, just as Christ loved us\f + \fr 5:2 \ft NE and WH \fqa Christ loved you\f* and gave Himself up for us as a fragrant sacrificial offering to God.
\p \v 3 But among you, as is proper among the saints, there must not be even a hint of sexual immorality, \add or\add* of any kind of impurity, or of greed. \v 4 \add Nor should there be\add* obscenity, foolish talk, or crude joking, which are out of character, but rather thanksgiving. \v 5 For of this you can be sure: \add No\add* immoral, impure, or greedy person (that is, an idolater) has \add any\add* inheritance in the kingdom of Christ and of God.
\p \v 6 \add Let\add* no one deceive you with empty words, for because of such things the wrath of God is coming on the sons of disobedience. \v 7 Therefore \add do\add* not be partakers with them.
\s1 Children of Light
\p \v 8 For you were once darkness, but now \add you are\add* light in \add the\add* Lord. Walk as children of light, \v 9 for the fruit of the light \add consists\add* in all goodness, righteousness, and truth. \v 10 Test and prove what pleases the Lord.
\p \v 11 Have no fellowship with the fruitless deeds of darkness, but rather expose \add them\add*. \v 12 For it is shameful even to mention what \add the disobedient\add* do in secret. \v 13 But everything exposed by the light becomes visible,\f + \fr 5:13 \ft SBL begins verse 14 after \fqa visible,\f* for everything that is illuminated becomes a light \add itself\add*. \v 14 So it is said:
\b 
\q1 “Wake up, O sleeper,
\q2 rise up from the dead,
\q2 and Christ will shine on you.”
\p \v 15 Pay careful attention, then, to how you walk, not as unwise but as wise, \v 16 redeeming the time, because the days are evil. \v 17 Therefore \add do\add* not be foolish, but understand what the Lord’s will \add is\add*. \v 18 \add Do\add* not get drunk on wine, which leads to reckless indiscretion. Instead, be filled with \add the\add* Spirit.
\p \v 19 Speak to one another with psalms, hymns, and spiritual songs. Sing and make music in your hearts to the Lord, \v 20 always giving thanks to God \add the\add* Father for everything in \add the\add* name of our Lord Jesus Christ.
\s1 Wives and Husbands
\r (\ref Song of Solomon 1:1–17|1:1-17\ref*; \ref 1 Peter 3:1–7|1PE 3:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 21 Submit to one another out of reverence for Christ.\f + \fr 5:21 \ft Or \fqa in the fear of Christ.\f*
\p \v 22 Wives, \add submit\add* to your husbands as to the Lord. \v 23 For \add the\add* husband is \add the\add* head of the wife as Christ \add is the\add* head of the church, \add His\add* body, \add of which\add* He \add is the\add* Savior. \v 24 Now as the church submits to Christ, so also wives \add should submit\add* to their husbands in everything.
\p \v 25 Husbands, love \add your\add* wives, just as Christ loved the church and gave Himself up for her \v 26 to sanctify her, cleansing \add her\add* by the washing with water through \add the\add* word, \v 27 \add and\add* to present her to Himself as a glorious church, without stain or wrinkle or any such \add blemish\add*, but holy and blameless.
\p \v 28 In the same way, husbands ought to love their wives as their own bodies. He who loves his wife loves himself. \v 29 Indeed, no one ever hated his \add own\add* body, but he nourishes and cherishes it, just as Christ \add does\add* the church. \v 30 For we are members of His body.\f + \fr 5:30 \ft BYZ and TR include \fqa —of His flesh and of His bones\ft .\f*
\p \v 31 “For this reason a man will leave his father and mother and be united to his wife, and the two will become one flesh.”\f + \fr 5:31 \ref Genesis 2:24|GEN 2:24\ref* (see also LXX)\f* \v 32 This mystery is profound, but I am speaking about Christ and the church. \v 33 Nevertheless, each one of you also must love his wife as \add he loves\add* himself, and the wife must respect \add her\add* husband.
\c 6
\s1 Children and Parents
\r (\ref Colossians 3:18–21|COL 3:18-21\ref*)
\p \v 1 Children, obey your parents in \add the\add* Lord, for this is right. \v 2 “Honor your father and mother” (which is the first commandment with a promise), \v 3 “that it may go well with you and \add that\add* you may have a long life on the earth.”\f + \fr 6:3 \ref Exodus 20:12|EXO 20:12\ref*; Deuteronomy 5:16\f*
\p \v 4 Fathers, \add do\add* not provoke your children \add to wrath\add*; instead, bring them up in \add the\add* discipline and instruction of \add the\add* Lord.
\s1 Serving with Honor
\r (\ref Colossians 3:22–25|COL 3:22-25\ref*; \ref 1 Timothy 6:1–2|1TI 6:1-2\ref*)
\p \v 5 Slaves, obey \add your\add* earthly masters with respect and fear \add and\add* sincerity of heart, just as \add you would obey \add* Christ. \v 6 \add And do this\add* not only to please them while they are watching, but as servants of Christ, doing the will of God from \add your\add* heart. \v 7 Serve with good will, as to the Lord and not to men, \v 8 because you know that \add the\add* Lord will reward each one for whatever good he does, whether \add he is\add* slave or free.
\p \v 9 And masters, do the same for \add your slaves\add*. Give up \add your\add* use of threats, because you know that \add He who is\add* both their Master and yours is in heaven, and there is no favoritism with Him.
\s1 The Full Armor of God
\p \v 10 Finally, be strong in \add the\add* Lord and in His mighty power. \v 11 Put on the full armor of God, so that you can make your stand against the devil’s schemes. \v 12 For our struggle is not against flesh and blood, but against the rulers, against the authorities, against the powers of this \add world’s\add* darkness, \add and\add* against the spiritual \add forces\add* of evil in the heavenly realms.
\p \v 13 Therefore take up the full armor of God, so that when the day of evil \add comes\add*, you will be able to stand your ground, and having done everything, to stand. \v 14 Stand firm then, with \add the belt of\add* truth buckled around your waist, \add with\add* the breastplate of righteousness arrayed, \v 15 and \add with your\add* feet fitted with \add the\add* readiness of the gospel of peace. \v 16 In addition to all \add this\add*, take up the shield of faith, with which you can extinguish all the flaming arrows of the evil one. \v 17 And take the helmet of salvation and the sword of the Spirit, which is \add the\add* word of God.
\p \v 18 Pray in \add the\add* Spirit at all times, with every kind of prayer and petition. To this \add end\add*, stay alert with all perseverance in your prayers for all the saints. \v 19 \add Pray\add* also for me, that whenever I open my mouth, words may be given me \add so that I will\add* boldly make known the mystery of the gospel, \v 20 for which I am an ambassador in chains. \add Pray\add* that I may proclaim it fearlessly, as I should.
\s1 Final Greetings
\r (\ref Philippians 4:21–23|PHP 4:21-23\ref*; \ref 2 Timothy 4:19–22|2TI 4:19-22\ref*)
\p \v 21 Tychicus, the beloved brother and faithful servant in \add the\add* Lord, will tell you everything, so that you also may know about me \add and\add* what I am doing. \v 22 I have sent \add him\add* to you for this very purpose, that you may know about us, and \add that\add* he may encourage your hearts.
\p \v 23 Peace to the brothers and love with faith from God \add the\add* Father and \add the\add* Lord Jesus Christ.
\p \v 24 Grace to all who love our Lord Jesus Christ with an undying \add love\add*.
